-- title:
--   Poincaré pullback of an O-point as a twist of sections
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and a Deligne–Rapoport package $\mathfrak P$ of level $N_0p$ over $R=\mathbb Z_{(p)}$, whose structure morphism $c:\mathfrak X\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ is assumed proper. Let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for $c$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $R$ with a zero section) and let $hD$ exhibit $D$ as representing the rigidified line bundles on $c$ with basepoint $\mathfrak P.\varepsilon_\infty$ that are fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero, with Poincaré bundle $hD.\mathrm{poincare}$; let $hDQ$ be the corresponding representability after base change to $\mathbb Q$, $hPQ$ an isomorphism between its Poincaré bundle and the base change to $\mathbb Q$ of the pullback of $hD.\mathrm{poincare}$ along the first projection, $ajQ$ a morphism over $\mathbb Q$ from the generic fibre of $c$ to $(D_{\mathbb Q}).P$, and $hajQ$ the Abel–Jacobi property of $ajQ$: for every field $K$, every $t:\operatorname{Spec}K\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Q$ and every $K$-point $x$ of the generic fibre, the Poincaré bundle pulled back along $x$ followed by $ajQ$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of $t$ followed by $\varepsilon_{\infty,\mathbb Q}$. Further data: a morphism $kQ$ from the fibre at $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the fibre at $\mathbb Q$ compatible with the first projections ($hkQ_1$), the geometric composite $\overline{aj}=\mathfrak P.\mathrm{eeta}\circ kQ\circ ajQ$ followed by the first projection, a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ lying over $\varepsilon_\infty$, and a bijection $\mathrm{pts}:J_0(N_0p)=\mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb Q},\ \text{modular function field})\to D(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ which is additive for the relative group law coming from $hD$ ($hpts\_add$) and pinned to $\overline{aj}$ in the sense that for geometric points $x,s$ of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ with $s$ over $\varepsilon_\infty$ there is a degree-zero divisor equal to $[\,\mathrm{place}(x)\,]-[\,\mathrm{place}(s)\,]$ whose class is sent by $\mathrm{pts}$ to $x$ followed by $\overline{aj}$ ($hpts\_aj$). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $eO$ an isomorphism of $O$ with the contraction of $A$ to the inertia fixed field of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$, with maximal ideal generated by $p$, let $\rho_O:R\to O$ be a ring homomorphism, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with $toκ:O\to k$, and $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ a resolved Deligne–Rapoport package for $\mathfrak P$ over $O$ relative to these data. Let $x$ be an inertia-invariant class in $J_0(N_0p)$, $D_0$ a degree-zero divisor representing it, $z$ an $O$-point of $D.P$ over $\rho_O$ whose restriction along the composite $O\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ determined by $eO$ is $\mathrm{pts}(x)$, $m$ a natural number with a bijection $idx$ of $\mathrm{Fin}\,m$ with the support of $D_0$, and $pos,neg:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathbb N$ with $pos_j-neg_j$ the multiplicity of $D_0$ at $idx_j$ and $\sum_j(pos_j-neg_j)=0$. Finally let $\sigma_j$ be sections of $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}O$ whose geometric generic points, transported through $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ and the first projection, are the points of $\mathfrak X$ attached to the places $idx_j$ by the package's point–place bijection. The conclusion is that on the generic fibre $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}\times_O\operatorname{Frac}O$ there is an isomorphism between the pullback along $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ and then the generic projection of the line bundle of $hD.\mathrm{poincare}$ pulled back along $z$, and the right-associated tensor product over $j\in\mathrm{Fin}\,m$, starting from the unit module, of the $pos_j$-th section twist of $\sigma_j$ (the inverse module of the $pos_j$-th power of the ideal of $\sigma_j$) tensored with the module of the $neg_j$-th power of that ideal.
--
--   This computes the specialisation to the resolved model of the Poincaré bundle classified by an $O$-point of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0p)$: on the generic fibre it is the divisorial twist $\bigotimes_j \mathcal O(pos_j\sigma_j - neg_j\sigma_j)$ attached to a degree-zero representative of the corresponding class. It supplies the generic-fibre half of the places-to-sections dictionary used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_sections_multidegree_eq_depth_of_exists_schemeHomOver_of_branch`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_sections_multidegree_eq_depth_of_exists_schemeHomOver_of_branch).
